#: ../../../devguide.rst:7
msgid "Build, setup and test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:9
msgid ""
"psutil makes extensive use of C extension modules, meaning a C compiler is "
"required, see :doc:`install instructions <install>`. Once installed run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:12
msgid ""
"git clone git@github.com:giampaolo/psutil.git\n"
"make install-sysdeps      # install gcc and python headers\n"
"make install-pydeps-test  # install test dependencies\n"
"make build\n"
"make install\n"
"make test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:21
msgid ""
"``make`` (via the :src:`Makefile`) is used for building, testing and general "
"development tasks, including on Windows (see below):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:24
msgid ""
"make clean\n"
"make install-pydeps-dev   # install dev deps (ruff, black, coverage, ...)\n"
"make test\n"
"make test-parallel\n"
"make test-memleaks\n"
"make test-coverage\n"
"make lint-all\n"
"make fix-all\n"
"make uninstall\n"
"make help"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:37
msgid "To run a specific test:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:39
msgid "make test ARGS=tests/test_system.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:43
msgid ""
"Do not use ``sudo``. ``make install`` installs psutil in editable mode, so "
"you can modify the code while developing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:46
msgid "To target a specific Python version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:48
msgid "make test PYTHON=python3.8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:53
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:55
msgid "The recommended way to develop on Windows is to use ``make``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:56
msgid ""
"Install `Git for Windows`_ and launch a *Git Bash shell*, which provides a "
"Unix-like environment where ``make`` works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:58
msgid "Then run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:60
msgid ""
"make build\n"
"make test-parallel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:68
msgid "Debug mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:70
msgid ""
"If you need to debug unusual situations or report a bug, you can enable "
"debug mode via the :envvar:`PSUTIL_DEBUG` environment variable. In this "
"mode, psutil may print additional information to stderr. Usually these are "
"non-severe error conditions that are ignored instead of causing a crash. "
"Unit tests automatically run with debug mode enabled. On UNIX:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:76
msgid ""
"$ PSUTIL_DEBUG=1 python3 script.py\n"
"psutil-debug [psutil/_psutil_linux.c:150]> setmntent() failed (ignored)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:81
msgid "On Windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:83
msgid ""
"set PSUTIL_DEBUG=1 && python.exe script.py\n"
"psutil-debug [psutil/arch/windows/proc.c:90]> "
"NtWow64ReadVirtualMemory64(...) -> 998 (Unknown error) (ignored)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:89
msgid "Coding style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:91
msgid ""
"All style and formatting checks are enforced locally on each ``git commit`` "
"and via a GitHub Actions pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:94
msgid ""
"Python: follows `PEP-8`_, formatted and linted with ``black`` and ``ruff``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:95
msgid "C: generally follows `PEP-7`_, formatted with ``clang-format``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:96
msgid ""
"Other files (``.rst``, ``.toml``, ``.md``, ``.yml``): validated by linters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:98
msgid "The pipeline re-runs all checks for consistency (``make lint-all``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:100
msgid ""
"Run ``make fix-all`` before committing; it usually fixes Python issues (via "
"``black`` and ``ruff``) and C issues (via ``clang-format``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:104
msgid "Code organization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:106
msgid ""
"psutil/__init__.py                   # Main API namespace (\"import "
"psutil\")\n"
"psutil/_common.py                    # Generic utilities\n"
"psutil/_ntuples.py                   # Named tuples returned by psutil APIs\n"
"psutil/_enums.py                     # Enum containers\n"
"psutil/_ps{platform}.py              # OS-specific python wrapper\n"
"psutil/_psutil_{platform}.c          # OS-specific C extension (entry "
"point)\n"
"psutil/arch/all/*.c                  # C code common to all OSes\n"
"psutil/arch/{platform}/*.c           # OS-specific C extension\n"
"tests/test_process|system.py         # Main system/process API tests\n"
"tests/test_{platform}.py             # OS-specific tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:120
msgid "Adding a new API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:122
msgid "Define the API in :src:`psutil/__init__.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:123
msgid ""
"Implement it in ``psutil/_ps{platform}.py`` (e.g. :src:`psutil/_pslinux.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:124
msgid "If needed, add C code in ``psutil/arch/{platform}/file.c``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:125
msgid ""
"Add a generic test in :src:`tests/test_system.py` or :src:`tests/"
"test_process.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devguide.rst:127
msgid "Add a platform-specific test in ``tests/test_{platform}.py``."
msgstr ""

